[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "ruy-b5 5.Bb3"]
[Name "5...d6: c3 before d4"]

5... d6 { Guards e5 and opens the c8 bishop. }
6. c3 { Prepares d4 and gives the bishop a way back to c2. Pushing 6.d4 at once is the road to the Noah's Ark Trap: after 6...Nxd4 7.Nxd4 exd4 the pawn on d4 looks free, and it costs the bishop on b3. [%cal Gc3d4] }
6... Nf6
7. O-O { Castles, and again leaves e4 for a moment, because taking it runs into a trick. [%idea castle-early] }
7... Be7 { A quiet developing move. }
( 7... Nxe4? { Takes a pawn, but it leaves two knights loose on the long light diagonal. [%csl Ye4,Yc6] }
  8. Bd5 { Hits both knights at once, and behind the one on c6 stands the rook on a8. [%cal Gd5e4,Gd5c6] [%idea fork] }
  8... Bb7 9. Bxe4 { The knight on e4 falls. }
  9... d5 10. Bc2 { The bishop steps back. White has won a knight for a pawn. } )
8. Re1 { Guards e4, and this is the closed main line: 8...O-O 9.h3 comes next. [%cal Ge1e4] } *
